# New-landing lattice

Read `components/marketing/landing-new/lattice/README.md` before adding or
changing sections. Summary of the hard rules:

- Every direct child of `<main data-lattice-root>` is a `LatticeSection`. Never
  insert a plain wrapper with its own height between sections.
- Size in cells: `LatticeCell cols={5} rows="auto" minRows={5}`. No
  `md:grid-cols-*`, no pixel widths, no fractional columns. Use `LatticeGrid
  minCols` for the stacking threshold, not Tailwind breakpoints.
- Spacing between lattice boxes only from `LATTICE_SPACE` in
  `lib/landingLattice.ts` (`sectionY`, `block`, …). Free spacing is allowed
  only inside a cell or plate.
- Headings/stats on the grid go in `LatticePlate`; card clusters in
  `LatticeGrid` with `stroke` (+ `equalRows` for one shared bottom line).
- Strokes: `latticeCellStrokeClassName` only. No `border`, `ring`, or
  `0 0 0 1px` shadows on lattice boxes.
- Full-bleed content inside a section uses `landingViewportBleedClassName` and
  measures its inset from the enclosing `[data-lattice-column]`; never
  hard-code column widths or gutters.
- Motion stays on the lattice too. A collapsing or sliding card may tween
  between sizes, but every rest pose (full cell or the 64×64 block) has edges
  ≡ 0 (mod 64) from the cell origin. No `left: 50%` / `translate(-50%)` pins
  that land on a half-cell.
- Do not import lattice primitives into `components/marketing/landing/*`
  paths used by `/`; extend shared components with opt-in props whose
  defaults keep `/` unchanged.

```tsx
// ✅ new section
<LatticeSection grid gridMask="fadeBoth" aria-labelledby="x">
  <LatticePlate><h2 id="x">…</h2></LatticePlate>
  <LatticeGrid className={LATTICE_SPACE.block} minCols={15} stroke equalRows>
    <LatticeCell cols={5} minRows={5}>…</LatticeCell>
  </LatticeGrid>
</LatticeSection>

// ❌ off the grid
<section className="py-24">
  <div className="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">…</div>
</section>
```

After layout changes, verify at 1440/1024/768/390 that section, plate, cell and
tile edges are ≡ 0 (mod 64) from the column left / root top (see README).
